// codebox_pass.gen -- f_wc stage 0: holds last frame's state (E, I), or reseeds it.
// 256x256 float32. Mirror: tests/modules/wc/wc_mirror.seed_state() (seeding); identity otherwise.
//
// Inputs: the first inlet is the `r draw` bang (unused; it only triggers the render every
// frame, and the feedback arrives on a cold inlet so it cannot retrigger the loop), the second
// is the feedback state (R = E, B = I, from the nl stage through the hold stage), the third is
// the noise texture (R = seed-E hash, G = seed-I hash, from the noise stage).
// reseed = 1 replaces the state with uniform noise in [0, amp): E from R, I from G (two
// independent hash channels), never zero and never uniform rest (it is a fixed point of the
// whole update, FR-004). reseed fires on load and on the reset trigger (FR-009).
//   - SELF-HEAL: a feedback texel that is exactly 0 in BOTH channels is reseeded from the
//     noise too. A live WC field never holds an exact 0 (E, I stay inside (0, 1): relaxation
//     toward a sigmoid output), so this fires only when the state was lost: a fresh module, a
//     GL context rebuilt by a window mode change, or a non-finite texel the nl stage zapped
//   - selection uses switch(), not mix(): mix(NaN, x, 1) is still NaN, so a poisoned feedback
//     texel could survive a reseed through mix
//   - the feedback is NaN/Inf-guarded: abs(x) < 1e30 (NaN == NaN is TRUE on this GPU)
//   - packing: R = E, B = I, G = A = 0 (G, A are the imaginary parts in the DFT chain; they
//     MUST stay 0 here)
Param reseed(0);
Param amp(1);

fbe = nearest(in2, norm).x;
fbe = switch(abs(fbe) < 1e30, fbe, 0);
fbi = nearest(in2, norm).z;
fbi = switch(abs(fbi) < 1e30, fbi, 0);
ze = nearest(in3, norm).x * amp;
zi = nearest(in3, norm).y * amp;
lost = (fbe == 0) * (fbi == 0);
kept_e = switch(lost > 0.5, ze, fbe);
kept_i = switch(lost > 0.5, zi, fbi);
out1 = vec(switch(reseed >= 0.5, ze, kept_e), 0, switch(reseed >= 0.5, zi, kept_i), 0);
